# .trivyignore — baseline for scripts/container-scan.sh (trivy 0.74.0).
# RULE: every entry carries a reason + date comment (project rule), and an
# `exp:` date so it EXPIRES LOUDLY instead of rotting — an expired entry makes
# the scan fail again (verified 2026-08-16 on trivy 0.74.0: future date
# suppresses, past date fires). Same expiry discipline as osv-scanner.toml's
# ignoreUntil. Anything NOT listed here fails the scan — that is the guard.

# --- Alpine base image baseline (2026-08-15) --------------------------------
# eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine (alpine 3.23.5, re-pulled and rescanned
# 2026-08-15): 14 OS-package CVEs (2 HIGH: libexpat, p11-kit; 12 MEDIUM),
# none in code we control. We do not chase base-image CVE zero (006 phase 5
# brief). REVISIT on every base-image refresh: libexpat's HIGH is fixed in
# 2.8.2-r0, so a future image build may clear several of these — shrink the
# list when they do.
CVE-2026-2100 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-50219 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56131 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56132 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56403 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56404 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56405 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56406 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56407 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56408 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56409 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56410 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56411 exp:2027-02-15
CVE-2026-56412 exp:2027-02-15

# --- JAR findings (2026-08-15) -----------------------------------------------
# FALSE POSITIVE: the lockfiles pin mssql-jdbc 12.10.2.jre11, which trivy's own
# fixed-version list for this CVE contains; trivy string-matches "12.10.2"
# without the .jre11 classifier. Nothing to fix. (2026-08-15)
CVE-2025-59250 exp:2027-02-15
# log4j-api 2.24.3 — present only as the log4j-to-slf4j facade (no log4j-core;
# the vulnerable MapMessage encoding path is never exercised). NOTE: the safety
# argument is CONDITIONAL on log4j-core staying absent — the exp date forces a
# re-triage rather than encoding that condition into a permanent ignore. Same
# triage as osv-scanner.toml's GHSA-qv9r-c865-cp47 entry. Retire when the
# Spring Boot BOM ships log4j2 >= 2.25.5. (2026-08-15)
CVE-2026-49844 exp:2027-02-15

# --- Egress proxy image baseline (2026-11-07, #845) ---------------------------
# envoyproxy/envoy:distroless-v1.40.2@sha256:09ca6f21… (the managed reads' egress proxy,
# deploy/compose.yml + the Helm chart): 22 findings, all in the distroless Debian 13 base's
# libc6 2.41-12+deb13u4 (8 LOW, 14 MEDIUM, 0 HIGH/CRITICAL), every one "affected" with NO fixed
# Debian 13 version yet — there is nothing to upgrade to. Exposure: the proxy runs no shell, no
# wordexp/strfmon/glob/iconv caller, no nscd, and resolves names through Envoy's own c-ares
# resolver, not the glibc stub resolver (CVE-2026-8674, CVE-2026-5435); its only clients are the
# app's DuckDB readers inside the deployment's network (no published port; the NetworkPolicy
# admits only the app pods). The Ubuntu-based tag carries 2 HIGH and was not chosen. REVISIT on
# the next Envoy release or when Debian ships a fixed libc6; the exp date forces the re-triage.
CVE-2010-4756 exp:2027-02-07
CVE-2018-20796 exp:2027-02-07
